acceptance_checks:
test_prod_recipe_builder checks that:
- recipe_sha256 and content_sha256 are identical across two builds with shuffled dict key order;
- changing only released_at or version leaves content_sha256 unchanged but changes recipe_sha256;
- one tolerance change changes content_sha256;
- the exact code sets are returned for a stale draft, unconfirmed order, an unconfirmed active mark, a missing drawing, missing tolerances and a manual mark without an angle;
- removed marks are absent from bends and present in removed_candidates;
- NATIVE_SWEEP target 90 gives included 90, and sweep 45 gives included 135.

test_prod_bend_identity checks that:
- the uid is stable under an endpoint swap and 1e-4 mm jitter;
- re-tagging an identical CAD remaps 100% matched;
- a bend moved 5 mm appears as removed + new;
- two symmetric parallel bends with a midway candidate are reported ambiguous and not assigned.

Durability test:
- enqueue, lease, then drop every object (simulated crash) and advance the clock past the lease TTL;
- a new LineStore + JobRunner on the same file requeues the job (attempts=1);
- a second expiry fails it with WORKER_INTERRUPTED;
- JOB_RECOVERED events exist;
- dedupe_key blocks a second job for the same scan + recipe.

Hotfolder test:
- a binary PLY appended in 3 chunks at poll_interval 0.05 s is ingested exactly once, and only after 3 stable polls;
- '.x.ply', 'a.ply.part' and 'a.tmp' are never ingested;
- sidecar_mode='required' waits for 'a.ply.done';
- a truncated PLY is quarantined with PLY_TRUNCATED;
- the same bytes under a new name give SCAN_DUPLICATE and no job;
- an UNMATCHED outcome gives a quarantine row plus a reason JSON;
- a file dropped while stopped is ingested by a new poller instance.

Runner test:
- a completed job carries a result_summary copied from the fake result;
- a CAD hash mismatch fails with RECIPE_CAD_HASH_MISMATCH and the fake worker's marker file is never created;
- request_cancel during a sleeping fake worker ends in cancelled within 3 s;
- postprocess exit 2 gives POSTPROCESS_ERROR carrying the message from postprocess_error.json.

Synthetic-scan test (seeds 1-5, spacing 0.5 mm, σ 0.05 mm, registration error ≤ 0.2 mm / 0.1°):
- flange |error| p95 ≤ 0.25 mm and max ≤ 0.40 mm;
- angle |error| ≤ 0.25°;
- as-built deltas of +2.0 mm, −2.0 mm and ±2° are recovered within the same bounds;
- outer-only and inner-only scans set the correct method flag and stay within 0.35 mm.

Honesty test:
- a far edge cropped by 20 mm → EDGE_NOT_OBSERVED with value None;
- an empty corridor → INSUFFICIENT_SUPPORT;
- the BOX_CORNER shared flange → FAR_BOUNDARY_AMBIGUOUS;
- a 178° included bend → DEGENERATE_ANGLE;
- no code path substitutes 0.0 or the nominal.

Binding test:
- shuffling the engine list gives the identical assignment;
- a deleted engine bend → UNBOUND;
- two parallel recipe bends 2 mm apart against one engine bend between them → AMBIGUOUS, unassigned;
- engine folded 135 against recipe included 45 is compatible.

chunks.goal:
Make the line deployable and safe on a shop-floor PC:
- validated configuration and a data root outside the repo;
- role-based access with station-scoped kiosk tokens;
- the currently unauthenticated legacy mutation routes closed in production mode;
- refusal to start with insecure defaults;
- structured logs, metrics and health;
- an immutable engine bundle that isolates runtime from mutable research files under output/.

acceptance_checks:
Settings test:
- a data root inside the repo, or under any data/ or output/ path → DATA_ROOT_INSIDE_REPO;
- SHERMAN_LINE_RSS_LIMIT_MB=20000 → RSS_LIMIT_INVALID;
- the SHERMAN_LINE_STATIONS JSON parses into StationConfig objects;
- a regex without 'sku' → FILENAME_REGEX_INVALID.

Route policy test on a stub ASGI app, with no legacy import:
- POST /api/auth/register → 403 by default, passes with allow_self_register;
- POST /api/parts → 401 without a token, 403 for viewer, passes for operator;
- DELETE /api/parts/x → 403 for operator, passes for admin;
- POST /api/live-scan/config → 403 when legacy live scan is disabled;
- GET /api/health is untouched.

Token tests:
- a device token for cell-1 verifies with station_scope cell-1 and has line.read only for cell-1;
- a revoked token → None;
- a stream token is rejected after its ttl and when tampered.

Bundle test on a synthetic mini repo in tmp_path. The repo has an entry file with a lazy function-level import of a backend module, a domains package, and decoys data/x.json and output/y.py.
- build copies the closure plus __init__ files and excludes the decoys;
- verify passes;
- editing a copied file makes verify report that file;
- bundle_id is identical across two builds.

chunks.goal:
Turn the existing catalog CAD/drawing upload plus Vendor Setup order tagging into a single gated release:
- a versioned, immutable PartRecipe frozen with copies of the CAD and drawing;
- registered as a benchmark reference;
- resolvable by SKU from a scan filename;
- with nominal expectations computed by the line.

acceptance_checks:
Route test on a minimal FastAPI app with only this router, overridden capability, a tmp PartCatalogManager holding a synthetic STL CAD + PDF and its bend specs, a confirmed draft saved with catalog.save_vendor_setup_draft, and a stubbed legacy context:
- POST /api/production/parts/{id}/recipe/release → 201 with recipe_id 'SYN-HAT-1@v1', bends in draft sequence order, and both CAD and drawing files present under <tmp root>/recipes/ by sha;
- an identical second POST → 200 'unchanged';
- a changed tolerance → 'SYN-HAT-1@v2' with supersedes_version 1;
- GET /api/production/recipes/by-sku/SYN-HAT-1 returns v2.

Gate tests return exact codes:
- catalog CAD republished after the draft was saved → 422 DRAFT_STALE;
- operator_sequence_confirmed false → SEQUENCE_NOT_CONFIRMED;
- one active mark pending → UNCONFIRMED_ACTIVE_MARKS;
- no drawing → DRAWING_MISSING;
- no tolerances → TOLERANCES_MISSING;
- expected_draft_revision mismatch → 409 DRAFT_REVISION_CHANGED;
- parts 'abc 1' and 'ABC-1' → 409 SKU_COLLISION.

Resolver test:
- 'SYN-HAT-1_SN7_20261017T101500.ply' → MATCHED with the active recipe id and sha;
- 'NOPE.ply' → UNMATCHED;
- a registered SKU with no recipe → PART_NOT_READY;
- a SKU with only retired versions → PART_NOT_READY.

chunks.goal:
Take the unchanged engine worker's outputs and the frozen recipe and produce:
- the per-bend expected-vs-actual result: flange A/B OML length, included angle and bend-line position, with tolerance conformance and honest NOT_MEASURED/INVALID states;
- decimated, index-aligned 3D assets for the station;
- the detailed PDF report.

acceptance_checks:
Honesty test:
- alignment_abstained=true → INVALID_INSPECTION, with every quantity NOT_MEASURED and reason INVALID_INSPECTION;
- transform scale 25.4 → UNIT_MISMATCH_SUSPECTED;
- one flange's far edge cropped → that quantity is EDGE_NOT_OBSERVED and the summary is INCOMPLETE;
- an engine match with assignment_source CAD_LOCAL_NEIGHBORHOOD never supplies an actual value;
- a fake engine angle 3° off yields METHOD_DISAGREEMENT.

PDF test, using fitz:
- the text contains the SKU, 'v1', every bend label in sequence order, 'Not measured' and 'Operator assist';
- no NOT_MEASURED row contains 'PASS';
- two renders of the same result are byte-identical.

chunks.goal:
Expose the durable line to the kiosk and to operators:
- a cheap pollable station feed and an SSE stream;
- strictly allowlisted per-job artifacts served outside the legacy OUTPUT_DIR;
- quarantine resolution, retry and cancel with audit events;
- device-token management;
- public readiness plus authenticated status and metrics.

acceptance_checks:
Feed and ETag:
- a completed job with a valid result in the tmp workspace → 200 with a validated result and artifact URLs;
- repeating with If-None-Match → 304;
- completing a newer job changes the ETag;
- a later failed job appears as latest_issue JOB_FAILED without replacing latest_completed.

Artifacts:
- only allowlisted names are served;
- '../job.json', 'recipe.json' and 'engine/bend_inspection_report.json' → 404;
- the f32 response has X-Deviation-Count equal to size/4;
- the PDF response has Content-Disposition attachment.

node frontend/react/scripts/check-station-view-model.mjs passes. It checks that:
- rows are sorted by sequence_index;
- NOT_MEASURED and NOT_APPLICABLE never receive pass/fail colours;
- deriveSummary equals every example's summary.state;
- validateResult rejects a copy with authority.mode changed, a copy claiming ALL_MEASURED_IN_TOLERANCE while a required quantity is NOT_MEASURED, and a NOT_MEASURED value that carries an actual;
- the heatmap colours at −band, 0 and +band equal the legend swatches.

When Chromium is available, node frontend/react/scripts/check-station-layout.mjs reports at 1920×1080:
- scrollWidth ≤ 1920 and scrollHeight ≤ 1080;
- table body font-size ≥ 20 px;
- viewer width ≥ 60% of the viewport;
- Heatmap off turns scan points to the neutral colour;
- clicking row 2 changes the camera target;
- a changed mocked ETag swaps the displayed job_id within 3 s without a reload.

Label test:
- uncertain → null;
- wrong_location → excluded;
- weak labels never appear in the evaluation truth column;
- no SKU family spans two splits.

Observable from a temporary app copy built with `env PYTHONPATH=.:backend .venv/bin/python -m apps.production_line.engine_bundle build --repo-root . --dest $TMPDIR/app --profile app`, never the dev repo:
- set SHERMAN_LINE_ENABLED=1, SHERMAN_LINE_DATA_ROOT=$TMPDIR/line and a station inbox under $TMPDIR;
- `python -m apps.production_line.server --port 9000` and `python -m apps.production_line.service_main --build-bundle` both start;
- `curl -s localhost:9000/api/line/health/ready` returns JSON {ready, checks};
- with SHERMAN_PRODUCTION_HARDENING=1 and SECRET_KEY unset, the server exits 2 naming SECRET_KEY_MISSING_OR_DEFAULT.

deferred:
Engine changes that touch user-modified engine files. Each one first needs an A/B comparison on the C12 synthetic scorecard and then an authorized physical protocol:
(a) a fixed-cell registration policy: turn off auto_scale for calibrated mm scanners (domains/bend/services/heatmap_evidence_service.py:167; backend/qc_engine.py:1409-1437) and abstain when flip hypotheses tie;
(b) feed recipe bends into run_progressive_bend_inspection instead of re-extracting them from the mesh (backend/bend_inspection_pipeline.py:3952-3966, 4012-4025);
(c) unfold the mesh detector's folded included angle (backend/feature_detection/bend_detector.py:1767-1771);
(d) per-flange local or datum-based alignment for fixtured robot cells.
Until then, the C06 validity gates detect a silent scale change and mark the inspection INVALID instead of reporting a result.
